 "web": "These barriers land on the same people at once. One mother of two in South Memphis: works full-time at about $14 an hour, which puts her just over TennCare's line for a parent ($2,277 a month for a family of three) *(our arithmetic: 14 × 40 × 52 ÷ 12 ≈ $2,427)*, and too short of money to buy insurance; she has no paid sick days; her apartment complex files evictions on a schedule; her car needs a repair and the lender down the street is licensed to charge up to 279.5% a year; her child's school is on a closure list; the air outside the school has a permit and an appeal pending. No one barrier decided her life. Together they set the price.",
